amaya (11.4.7+modern5) noble; urgency=medium

  * Print to a PDF file (with Ghostscript); the print dialog asks before
    overwriting an existing file.
  * Print SVG drawings written with a namespace prefix (<svg:svg>).
  * SVG text: the caret no longer disappears when the text grows or after
    a zoom; arrow keys keep the caret in the text being edited.
  * Fix a crash when editing alternately in the source and formatted views.
  * SVG: indentation no longer grows at each source view synchronization.

 -- JoseMCruz <jmcruz2k21@gmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000

amaya (11.4.7+modern4) noble; urgency=medium

  * SVG text: a second click on a text of a selected group puts the caret
    in it; the caret is visible in drawings scaled by a viewBox; a click
    places it at the character under the mouse.
  * Connect the SVG, XML and Template callbacks: in SVG documents the
    source view is synchronized when going back to the formatted view.
  * Printing: MathML symbols and other characters that the printer fonts
    lack are printed as glyph outlines (the job was rejected before).

 -- JoseMCruz <jmcruz2k21@gmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

amaya (11.4.7+modern3) noble; urgency=medium

  * SVG editing: typing in a text inside a group (e.g. a LibreOffice Draw
    label) is no longer lost; no huge scrolling width with a viewBox, no
    jump after saving; saving no longer adds line breaks in text elements.
  * SVG printing: drawings are converted to EPS with librsvg and included
    in the PostScript output (new dependency on librsvg).
  * Printing: long picture file names; clean exit of the print helper;
    included EPS files wrapped in %%BeginDocument/%%EndDocument.

 -- JoseMCruz <jmcruz2k21@gmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000

amaya (11.4.7+modern2) noble; urgency=medium

  * SVG drawings (e.g. exported by LibreOffice Draw):
    - line widths follow the scaling of the drawing;
    - text in tspans nested in tspans is placed at its x and y;
    - text reduced by a scaling keeps all its strokes;
    - zooming no longer scales drawings with a viewBox twice.

 -- JoseMCruz <jmcruz2k21@gmail.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000

